@*
  Minimal layout used when a request is AJAX-driven by the dashboard's
  fragment-swap navigation (X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest).

  Why it exists: when Layout = null, the page body is rendered without any
  surrounding chrome — including _DashAlerts, which reads TempData and fires
  toast notifications for flash messages. Without this layout, TempData set
  by a POST never reaches the user until they manually refresh the page (at
  which point the full _DashboardLayout renders the partial).

  This shim ensures every AJAX fragment also includes the alerts partial,
  so success/error toasts appear immediately after a save.
*@
<partial name="_DashAlerts" />
@RenderBody()
@await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
